{"ts": 1791255622.1033869, "type": "step", "step": 10, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/evaluation.md", "section": "Evaluating agents"}, "output": "# Evaluating agents\n\n## pass@k vs pass^k\npass@k: any of k runs succeeds. pass^k: all k succeed. Reliability is what deployment needs.\n\n## Proxy vs direct measures\nA quiz score is a proxy. Retention a week later is closer to the thing itself.\n", "t": 0, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20987799811012606, "pomdp": 0.20987799811012606, "pass_k": 0.20987799811012606}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7900005928827397, "motivation": 0.8945163589496804, "reliance": 0.4367297305194162, "persistence": 0.33045379926157714, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.30772234089151984, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.275207256822714, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 0.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255622.104071, "type": "step", "step": 11, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "environments.md"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 0, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20987799811012606, "pomdp": 0.20987799811012606, "pass_k": 0.20987799811012606}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7900005928827397, "motivation": 0.8945163589496804, "reliance": 0.4367297305194162, "persistence": 0.33045379926157714, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.30772234089151984, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.275207256822714, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 0.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255623.548799, "type": "step", "step": 12, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I found the Friday build requirements: you need to define the environment (state, observations, actions, dynamics) and report pass^k on at least 3 seeds. I also found the relevant Week 3 readings on environments and evaluation.\n\nLet\u2019s use the session well. First, read the environments reading, then the evaluation reading. After that I\u2019ll quiz you briefly and help you turn it into your own build plan.\n\nStart here: Week 3 / environments.md, especially the sections on what an environment is, partial observability, and attention as a hidden variable.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-environments"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok got it, thanks\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pomdp?\n[activity] t=0 messages 2m", "t": 2, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20987799811012606, "pomdp": 0.3074871547195222, "pass_k": 0.20987799811012606}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7900005928827397, "motivation": 0.8945163589496804, "reliance": 0.45672973051941623, "persistence": 0.33045379926157714, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.30772234089151984, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.275207256822714, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255624.889845, "type": "step", "step": 13, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can\u2019t just hand over a one-word answer, but I can help you get there fast: a POMDP is a partially observable Markov decision process. In plain terms, it\u2019s an environment where the agent can\u2019t directly see the full state, so it has to act based on observations and often maintain a belief about what state it\u2019s in.\n\nTry saying it back in your own words in one sentence. If you want, I\u2019ll check it and help tighten it for your build notes.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-environments"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok got it, thanks\n[activity] t=2 messages 4m", "t": 6, "activity": [{"t": 2, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20987799811012606, "pomdp": 0.404323346609054, "pass_k": 0.20987799811012606}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7900005928827397, "motivation": 0.8945163589496804, "reliance": 0.45672973051941623, "persistence": 0.33045379926157714, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.30772234089151984, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.275207256822714, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
